{
  "title": "TKA Polyethylene Wear & Manufacturing",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/recon/5002/tka-polyethylene-wear-and-manufacturing",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Feb 28 2026",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "Summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "TKA polyethylene wear refers to macroscopic premature failure of polyethylene (PE) due to excessive loading and mechanical loosening",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is generally made with plain radiographs of the knee showing narrowing of the tibiofemoral implant interface",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment generally involves revision TKA or isolated polyethylene exchange depending on the stability of the femoral and tibial implants",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Incidence",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "catastrophic failure is most commonly seen in TKA",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "in contrast to osteolytic failure that is usually seen in THA",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "catastrophic failure may occur in TSA and THA replacement, but less common",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "primary variables that lead to catastrophic wear include:",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**PE thickness**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**articular surface design and geometry**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "flat PE should be avoided as knee loads exceed yield strength of UHMWPE in a flat design",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "goals of PE design:",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "maximize contact area",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "minimize contact loads (force/area)",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "biplanar congruency is the best design",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "text": "**congruent in both coronal and sagittal planes**",
                              "table": null,
                              "images": [],
                              "importance": "4",
                              "children": []
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "**kinematics**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "sliding wear is bad for PE",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "occurs when ACL is sacrificed and PCL remains",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "text": "most pronounced with CR knee design with a flat PE insert",
                              "table": null,
                              "images": [],
                              "importance": "2",
                              "children": []
                            },
                            {
                              "text": "**least pronounced with PS or AS knee design with a congruent PE insert**",
                              "table": null,
                              "images": [],
                              "importance": "4",
                              "children": []
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "**PE sterilization**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**PE manufacturing**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**surgical technique**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "tight flexion gap hastens sliding wear effect",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "tight PCL and anterior tibial slope amplify stress",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Polyethylene thickness",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Introduction",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "PE insert thickness can be variable depending on manufacturer definition (i.e. some may list PE thickness as the combined thickness of the insert + tibial tray)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "PE insert labeled as 8 mm, may only have a \"true\" PE thickness of 4-5 mm at the thinnest point with a ~3 mm thick metal tray",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Cause of failure",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**PE thickness <8 mm**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "leads to loads transmitted to localized area of PE that exceed PE's inherent yield strength (12-20 mPA)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "thickness of <8 mm associated with catastrophic PE failure",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "data based on older studies/PE generations, may not be as applicable with modern manufacturing",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Solution",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "maintain thinnest portion of PE >8 mm",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "a more aggressive tibial cut may avoid having to use a PE insert of <8 mm",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "in younger patients, increased activity combined with thinner PE will increase risk of catastrophic failure",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Articular surface design and geometry",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Introduction",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "two general designs in total knee prosthesis include:",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "a deeper **congruous** joint (deeper cut PE) without rollback",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "less anatomic",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**maximizes contact loads**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**decreases contact stress**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "a **flat** tibial PE that improves femoral rollback and optimizes flexion",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "more anatomic",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "PCL sparing",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**increases contact stress** and risk of catastrophic failure",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Cause of failure",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "flat designs of tibia PE",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "low contact surface area leads to high contact stress loads in areas of contact",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Solution",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**increase congruency of articular design**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "higher contact surface area leads to lower contact stress load",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "newer prosthesis designs sacrifice rollback and have a more congruent (\"dished\") fit between the femoral condyle and the tibial insert in both the sagittal and coronal planes to decrease the contact stress",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Kinematics",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Introduction",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "variables that affect kinetics include",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "knee alignment",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "varus alignment of knee associated with catastrophic PE failure",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "femoral rollback",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "optimizes flexion at the cost of increasing contact stress and increased risk of catastrophic failure",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Cause of failure",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**excessive femoral rollback**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "dyskinetic sliding movements of femur on tibia causes surface cracking and wear",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Solution",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "perform adequate bone cuts and/or releases to avoid varus malalignment",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "decrease contact stress by minimizing femoral rollback",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "use a more congruous joint design",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "increase posterior slope of tibia",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "use PCL substituting knee for incompetent PCL or dyskinetic femoral rollback",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "to compensate for the lack of rollback, newer designs move the point of contact (where femoral condyle rests) more posterior and have a steeper posterior slope to aid with flexion",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Polyethylene sterilization",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiation",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "gamma radiation is the most common form of polyethylene sterilization",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "results in oxidized PE that wears poorly and results in osteolysis",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "oxidation vs. cross-linking",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "presence of oxygen determines pathway following free radical formation",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**oxygen rich environment**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "PE becomes oxidized",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "text": "leads to early failure due to",
                              "table": null,
                              "images": [],
                              "importance": "5",
                              "children": [
                                {
                                  "text": "subsurface delamination",
                                  "table": null,
                                  "images": [],
                                  "importance": "5",
                                  "children": []
                                },
                                {
                                  "text": "pitting",
                                  "table": null,
                                  "images": [],
                                  "importance": "5",
                                  "children": []
                                },
                                {
                                  "text": "fatigue strength/cracking",
                                  "table": null,
                                  "images": [],
                                  "importance": "5",
                                  "children": []
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**oxygen depleted environment**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "PE becomes cross-linked",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "text": "improved **resistance to adhesive and abrasive wear**",
                              "table": null,
                              "images": [],
                              "importance": "5",
                              "children": []
                            },
                            {
                              "text": "**decrease in mechanical properties (decreased ductility and fatigue resistance)**",
                              "table": null,
                              "images": [],
                              "importance": "4",
                              "children": []
                            },
                            {
                              "text": "greater risk of catastrophic failure under high loads",
                              "table": null,
                              "images": [],
                              "importance": "2",
                              "children": []
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "methods to obtain",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "text": "**packing** via argon, nitrogen",
                              "table": null,
                              "images": [],
                              "importance": "4",
                              "children": []
                            },
                            {
                              "text": "packing in vacuum environment",
                              "table": null,
                              "images": [],
                              "importance": "2",
                              "children": []
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "removal of free radicals",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "thermal stabilization/remelting",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "removes free radicals formed during the radiation sterilization process for cross-linking",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "most effective means of removing free radicals as it occurs above the PE melting point",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "changes the PE from its partial crystalline state to its amorphous state",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "disadvantage is that it **reduces the mechanical properties** of the material",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "5",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "annealing",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "maintains its mechanical property",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**less effective at removing free radicals as it occurs below the PE melting point**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "leaves the PE more susceptible to oxidation",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Solution",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "irradiate PE in inert gas or vacuum to minimize oxidation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Polyethylene manufacturing",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Introduction",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "cutting tools can disrupt chemical bonds of PE",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Fabrication methods",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**ram bar extrusion and machining**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "UHMWPE powder fed into heated chamber, ram pushes powder into heated cylinder barrel forming a cylindrical rod, cut into 10 ft lengths for sale",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "implants are machined from the cylindrical bar stock",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "leads to variations in PE quality within the bar",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**calcium stearate additive**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "leads to fusion defects in PE",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**sheet compression molding**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "UHMWPE powder introduced into large 4' x 8' rectangular container to make sheets up to 8\" thick",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "implants are machined from these molded sheets",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**direct compression molding/net shape**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "best PE fabrication process",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "UHMWPE powder placed into a mold the shape of the final component, which is heated",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "the net shape implant is removed and packaged",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "no external machining involved, implants have high gloss surface finish",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "lower wear rates (50% wear rate of machined products)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "slow, expensive",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Cause of failure",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**machining shear forces** cause subsurface region (1-2 mm) stretching of PE chains",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "especially in amorphous regions > crystalline regions",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "PE chains are more susceptible to radiation resulting in greater oxidation in this region",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "leads to subsurface delamination and fatigue cracking",
